<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:56:05Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Ukraine live: Romania probes possible drone attack on tanker</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6002d68aa1cde4da2c1a542d8fe5587731fedc18bc228fb0cbb3817fd601b8a0</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:54:20Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T03:52:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-ukraine-live-romania-probes-possible-drone-attack-on-tanker--ecf4ed2542dc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-ukraine-live-romania-probes-possible-drone-attack-on-tanker" /><summary type="html">Romania on Wednesday was probing a possible fresh drone attack on a tanker off its Black Sea coast. Suspected Russian drones have hit several ships off Romania and neighbouring Bulgaria since last week in the latest spillover from the Ukraine war in the Black Sea. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Albania protests turn violent as protestors demand PM Rama's resignation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ca146e35844905be07e540e31bd3e6d440435682cd9df797b18b17c82a70e46b</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:54:32Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T22:35:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-albania-protests-protestors-demand-pm-rama-resignation--fc3550df0859.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-albania-protests-protestors-demand-pm-rama-resignation" /><summary type="html">Anti-government protests in Albania’s capital Tirana turned violent for a second consecutive night on Wednesday, leaving several government buildings damaged and at least one ablaze. Thousands demanded Prime Minister Edi Rama’s resignation and improved university conditions. Police fired tear gas and deployed water cannons as protesters smashed windows and attacked buildings.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>French anti-terror investigators probe True Crime Community link to school shooting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:49e2773fee44d52a38da34a81d7f95dac124f5fa66b13337ff7f1397117f25e3</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:54:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T21:01:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261014-french-anti-terror-investigators-probe-true-crime-community-link-to-school-shooting--786227e648c5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261014-french-anti-terror-investigators-probe-true-crime-community-link-to-school-shooting" /><summary type="html">The French anti-terrorism prosecutor has taken ​over the investigation into a school shooting near Marseille, after an initial probe found the 14-year-old suspect appeared to belong to ​a ‌group called the True Crime ⁠Community. Two teachers were shot and wounded, after a student opened fire with ⁠a hunting rifle that had been hidden inside a guitar case. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Alexandre Rodde, security consultant, researcher and author of the report "Understanding nihilistic violent extremism and the True Crime Community in France".</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>French anti-terror investigators probe True Crime Community link to school shooting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3b9d9366d7d05527a8a089292a1df115a607dbdc188fe1ebc0a6b7c49447ae62</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:54:41Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T20:58:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/french-anti-terror-investigators-probe-true-crime-community-link-to-school-shooting--965e949188ad.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/french-anti-terror-investigators-probe-true-crime-community-link-to-school-shooting" /><summary type="html">The French anti-terrorism prosecutor has taken ​over the investigation into a school shooting near Marseille, after an initial probe found the 14-year-old suspect appeared to belong to ​a ‌group called the True Crime ⁠Community. Two teachers were shot and wounded, after a student opened fire with ⁠a hunting rifle that had been hidden inside a guitar case. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Alexandre Rodde, security consultant, researcher and author of the report "Understanding nihilistic violent extremism and the True Crime Community in France".</summary></entry><entry><title>What is Starshield, SpaceX's military version of Starlink?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:248f7f7f316eb01c318d5287dd51ab3102289558d94528f4f2a6b0b07653fadd</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:54:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T20:15:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-what-is-starshield-spacex-s-military-version-of-starlink--420f2336136c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-what-is-starshield-spacex-s-military-version-of-starlink" /><summary type="html">Elon Musk’s ⁠SpaceX restricted “military-grade” ​Starlink services overnight into Wednesday, hampering Ukrainian drone strike missions and air defenses, Ukraine reported. In response, Musk said that the US government was behind any slowdown in Ukraine's Starshield system.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Nord Stream may have been lawful target, argue lawyers for Ukrainian accused of bombing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:78d698e21566cf7aae438399aa003710ec0c2570d9f533a99def50173e5b259e</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:54:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T19:56:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nord-stream-may-have-been-lawful-target-argue-lawyers-for-ukrainian-accused-of-bombing--ce42ad081609.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nord-stream-may-have-been-lawful-target-argue-lawyers-for-ukrainian-accused-of-bombing" /><summary type="html">Lawyers for a Ukrainian ex-military officer accused of leading the bombing of Russia's Nord Stream ​pipeline in September 2022 argued at the start of his trial in Germany on Wednesday that "an aggressor's infrastructure" may have been a lawful target. FRANCE 24's Juliette Brown reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Starlink restriction 'no surprise' after Musk condemned Ukraine strikes on Russian data centres</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c11575afdb81b30f36811be31d695b3c5dfc8c1d63d03b3995860236b1742f2a</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:54:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T19:49:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/starlink-restriction-no-surprise-after-musk-condemned-ukraine-strikes-on-russian-data-centres--fd09c9bb9e0f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/starlink-restriction-no-surprise-after-musk-condemned-ukraine-strikes-on-russian-data-centres" /><summary type="html">Restrictions reported by Ukraine on its use of the US satellite internet system Starlink have exposed Kyiv's reliance on the technology for both offensive and defensive operations in its fight against Russia'a invasion, analysts and observers say. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, David Galbreath Professor of War and Technology at the University of Bath, says that "we always knew that allowing a private organisation like Starlink to have such a big impact on the combat operations in Ukraine was going to be challenging", explaining that "it is no surprise" that Starlink services had been throttled after SpaceX boss Elon Musk called the targeting by Ukrainian drones of data services in Russia "a step too far".</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine says Starlink restricted operations overnight, disrupting military missions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b488f6ef0d4f09e558ebfd9e035faebd22f60beb4d442d0c050997be5295ae75</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:55:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T09:14:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-ukraine-says-starlink-restricted-operations-overnight-disrupting-military-missions--3220e9df249a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-ukraine-says-starlink-restricted-operations-overnight-disrupting-military-missions" /><summary type="html">Elon Musk's Starlink imposed restrictions on the operation of internet terminals in Ukraine overnight, disrupting military missions, an adviser to the Ukrainian president said on Wednesday. The official said Ukraine was given no prior warning about the restrictions to the satellite system it relies on for battlefield operations.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Trump says 'massive' oil, gas and mineral exploration to begin in Greenland</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5b913f2686816596d1fb34034f1c6d382f49e71144295856adfde01399b954b4</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:55:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T06:41:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-trump-says-massive-oil-gas-and-mineral-exploration-to-begin-in-greenland--f4d2d91425e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-trump-says-massive-oil-gas-and-mineral-exploration-to-begin-in-greenland" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump said on Wednesday that a "massive" oil, gas and mineral exploration was slated to begin in Greenland. The US, Denmark and Greenland last month signed a security agreement after Trump's repeated threats to seize control of the island.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Trial lawyer for Ukrainian accused of sabotage says Russia used Nord Stream as a ‘weapon’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5cf305a2b555c896fbd7c168122ab5073aabbe74164add43de86a91abe4558ba</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:55:51Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T06:37:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-defence-of-ukrainian-accused-of-sabotage-says-russia-used-nord-stream-pipelines-as-weapon--ab78193a18b6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-defence-of-ukrainian-accused-of-sabotage-says-russia-used-nord-stream-pipelines-as-weapon" /><summary type="html">The Nord Stream gas pipelines were a political and economic “weapon” for Russia, the lawyer for former Ukrainian officer Sergei Kuznetsov said Wednesday. The first to appear in the high-profile case, Kuznetsov is accused by German prosecutors of having led the plan to sabotage the infrastructure in 2022.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>US government behind any slowdown in Ukraine's Starshield system, Musk says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b71ba6dd40b2822730fd1a480d201c8cf51b923145b965f22e40c12a49207b1e</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:55:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T06:19:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-live-ukraine-massive-russian-attack-on-energy-facilities-at-least-six-dead--c9372a6d0ab2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-live-ukraine-massive-russian-attack-on-energy-facilities-at-least-six-dead" /><summary type="html">SpaceX boss Elon Musk said Wednesday that any disruptions in the Starshield satellite communications system would be the responsibility of the US government, not his company. Earlier, Ukraine’s President Volodymyr Zelensky called on Musk to “switch on” the system which Kyiv relies on for communications and logistics. Read our blog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>What we know about Pope Leo XIV's lung cancer diagnosis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f9b8e2f99cf424ffc4991e33b2aabb91ed77a7eff6fad3453a3209027a7a47a9</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:55:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T03:35:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-what-we-know-about-pope-leo-xiv-s-lung-cancer-operation--ea1d8bfcf529.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-what-we-know-about-pope-leo-xiv-s-lung-cancer-operation" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo underwent surgery on Tuesday to remove a cancerous tumour from his right lung after saying that a nodule had been "detected at a very early stage". Following a "successful" operation, the Vatican said the 71-year-old pontiff would undergo additional testing.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Kyiv power plant hit by Russian missile without warning from allies</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e520d5a788e53b051b8a731f1c6ec6c418d72bf82c8279fc13130f863fa1ee56</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:55:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T00:41:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-kyiv-power-plant-hit-by-russian-missile-without-warning-from-allies--dd9577fe7ac1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-kyiv-power-plant-hit-by-russian-missile-without-warning-from-allies" /><summary type="html">Ukraine's President Volodymyr Zelensky said Tuesday that a Russian ballistic missile struck a Kyiv power plant without advance warning from Western allies, killing at least two people and wounding around 20. The attack came days after US President Donald Trump announced an energy ceasefire between Moscow and Kyiv, raising questions over efforts to halt strikes on critical infrastructure.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo has cancerous growth removed in lung operation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3ba6162f9968789111b9fa3c2d9907d300361f0b9c2cf625df96129b72153edf</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:56:02Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T21:23:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/pope-leo-has-cancerous-growth-removed-in-lung-operation--898967a682f5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/pope-leo-has-cancerous-growth-removed-in-lung-operation" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo XIV had a cancerous growth removed from his right lung in a 90-minute operation on Tuesday and "woke up normally" after the procedure, the Vatican said. A Vatican source said further tests were being carried out to determine if the cancer had spread. "To ensure the procedure was radical, the lower lobe of the right lung was removed," the Vatican said in a statement. FRANCE 24's Seema Gupta reports from Rome.</summary></entry><entry><title>Have Ukrainian strikes on Yandex data centres hit Russian online disinformation?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a8bf627548259be073737a07e952d1df8094ac557065245e3eaa832d697667d2</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:56:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T20:59:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261013-have-ukrainian-strikes-on-yandex-data-centres-hit-russian-online-disinformation--2dc555b32969.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261013-have-ukrainian-strikes-on-yandex-data-centres-hit-russian-online-disinformation" /><summary type="html">After recent Ukrainian bombings of Russian data centres belonging to Yandex, internet users claim to have noticed a sharp reduction in pro-Russian and far-right populist social media content. They suggest the reduction is a direct result of the strikes cutting off Russian disinformation "bots". We examine the claim in this edition of Truth or Fake.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Ceuta an 'inalienable' part of Spain, king says on key visit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1cd2a6ed810def17d8d40c0f67fbefd5f627f48bf20c582b09398eac8a1007f6</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:53:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T19:06:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ceuta-an-inalienable-part-of-spain-king-says-on-key-visit--84d6778d9333.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ceuta-an-inalienable-part-of-spain-king-says-on-key-visit" /><summary type="html">King Felipe VI on Tuesday said Ceuta and Melilla were "an inalienable part" of Spain as he made a landmark visit to the north African territories claimed by neighbouring Morocco. "Ceuta and Melilla are an inalienable part of the political and national reality that is Spain. The sovereignty and territorial integrity of our country are not negotiable," Felipe said. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris reports from Madrid.</summary></entry><entry><title>King Felipe VI says Ceuta is ‘inalienable’ part of Spain in landmark visit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:48b9ae16750b28946e2d1380c6e68ed1b08b8de196cf56318cf52baca041d0f2</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:53:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T15:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261013-spanish-royals-visit-ceuta-amid-tensions-with-morocco-over-migrant-influx--f9df8bcf336a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261013-spanish-royals-visit-ceuta-amid-tensions-with-morocco-over-migrant-influx" /><summary type="html">King Felipe VI and Queen Letizia visited Ceuta on Tuesday for the first time in 14 years, with the monarch reaffirming Spain’s sovereignty over the North African enclaves claimed by Morocco. The landmark visit comes amid strained relations with Rabat and the aftermath of a mass migrant influx that saw makeshift camps cleared ahead of the royals’ arrival.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Belgium: Greener schools thanks to European funding</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:696200fa801cbbdd6a99ed659aef3c1a6fba5c919d26f5bb5861379d023299b0</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:53:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T14:27:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/belgium-greener-schools-thanks-to-european-funding--c7570949caa0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/belgium-greener-schools-thanks-to-european-funding" /><summary type="html">🇧🇪 In Ganshoren, in Belgium, a new school replaces run-down buildings. But the need for renovations remains enormous.👉🏻 Find the whole reporting on France 24 English.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia pounds Ukrainian cities, spares energy targets for first time since Trump 'ceasefire'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1d9f534686a98ce0cf755b507ec961cb92df37386dc141b4175373b44bc26dc6</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:53:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T13:39:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261013-russia-pounds-ukrainian-cities-spares-energy-targets-for-first-time-since-trump-ceasefire--9892d97dd176.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261013-russia-pounds-ukrainian-cities-spares-energy-targets-for-first-time-since-trump-ceasefire" /><summary type="html">Russia hammered Ukrainian cities and transport links overnight into Tuesday, killing at least four people in the city of Kharkiv, while appearing to spare energy facilities for the first time since US President Donald Trump announced an "energy ceasefire" at the weekend. It was not clear whether Moscow had deliberately avoided targeting power plants.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Spanish royals visit crisis-hit Ceuta amid diplomatic tensions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8dc04b9ddc4589ff05aea4e5fb71cb609d4af5921ee8b141eeac7161622669ae</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:53:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T13:30:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/spanish-royals-visit-crisis-hit-ceuta-amid-diplomatic-tensions--bc891a439a35.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/spanish-royals-visit-crisis-hit-ceuta-amid-diplomatic-tensions" /><summary type="html">Spain’s King Felipe VI and Queen Letizia visited Ceuta for the first time since 2007, amid tensions with Morocco following July’s migration crisis, when more than 70,000 people crossed into the Spanish enclave. Most returned to Morocco, but thousands remained, and dozens died. Morocco claims sovereignty over Ceuta, making the royal visit diplomatically sensitive. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris has more from Madrid.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Transactional diplomacy': Greece positioning itself as Trump's most 'reliable ally in the region'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d481c7ac896035eea8a74fa1e9c073da2ca32e5cefab4ef9cfd4583e51c65749</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:53:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T11:41:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261013-transactional-diplomacy-greece-positioning-itself-as-the-us-most-reliable-ally-in-the-regio--4880927fce4d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261013-transactional-diplomacy-greece-positioning-itself-as-the-us-most-reliable-ally-in-the-region" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Petros Konstantinidis, a financial journalist for Greece's leading daily newspaper TA NEA. The current controversy surrounding the US ambassador to Greece, Kimberly Guilfoyle, has all the makings of a reality TV show or a telenovela, or both. "This is diplomacy under Trump turning into lifestyle diplomacy," Konstantinidis explains.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Spain’s king visits Ceuta amid tensions with Morocco</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:286373f71a5a6ee5d34f596f3341ae8395449ac297416fdb96fbba6815576e71</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:53:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T09:22:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/spain-s-king-visits-ceuta-amid-tensions-with-morocco--a4c4f2800cac.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/spain-s-king-visits-ceuta-amid-tensions-with-morocco" /><summary type="html">King Felipe VI and Queen Letizia are visiting Ceuta months after more than 70,000 migrants arrived from Morocco. While most have returned, thousands remain. The visit has divided residents and risks reigniting diplomatic tensions with Morocco, which claims sovereignty over Ceuta and Melilla.</summary></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo XIV admitted to hospital for lung surgery</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:83c27886707e986990f870e29608c2071c5ea4c7f4b5faa6be3847e74d66a13e</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:53:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T09:20:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/pope-leo-xiv-admitted-to-hospital-for-lung-surgery--7eb0dd11a883.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/pope-leo-xiv-admitted-to-hospital-for-lung-surgery" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo XIV has been admitted to Rome’s Gemelli hospital for surgery to remove a small lung nodule discovered during recent medical checks. The 71-year-old pontiff said the growth was detected at an early stage. The procedure marks his first hospitalisation since becoming pope in May 2025. FRANCE 24's Seema Gupta has the latest from Rome.</summary></entry><entry><title>French students ‘not giving up the fight’ as 480,000 join new day of school protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1b2329afc76ccba445800d77ef4922ce410ccdac3645cb39ba23d5362d8b02db</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:53:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T06:44:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261013-live-france-braces-for-fresh-nationwide-protests-over-school-conditions--ed166873d347.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261013-live-france-braces-for-fresh-nationwide-protests-over-school-conditions" /><summary type="html">French students staged another day of nationwide protests on Tuesday over poor school conditions, including teacher shortages and dilapidated buildings, vowing to keep up the pressure ahead of half-term holidays. Around 480,000 protesters joined in on the demonstrations, with Swedish activist Greta Thunberg turning up in Paris to boost the movement’s visibility. Read our liveblog to see how all the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'A positive step': Hungary removes anti-LGBTQ provisions from Orban-era law</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:35cc489bdbfa7212412562e30f03d633935f7c6b56baaa493d0367529521d0b5</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:53:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T05:15:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261013-a-positive-step-hungary-removes-anti-lgbtq-provisions-from-orban-era-law--b96f27471fa6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261013-a-positive-step-hungary-removes-anti-lgbtq-provisions-from-orban-era-law" /><summary type="html">Hungary's parliament voted on Tuesday to remove anti-LGBTQ provisions from a "child protection" law adopted in 2021 under the country's former nationalist leader, in the first significant move to reverse discriminatory legislation since Prime Minister Peter Magyar took power in May.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russia says Europe bought $320 billion in hydrocarbons since 2022</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:206184a7491df0dee6680db51fab9c1feb2f86c0c6d36979a75791da4f7c9dc9</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:53:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T03:10:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261013-russia-says-europe-bought-320-billion-in-hydrocarbons-since-2022--d9b66d1b054f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261013-russia-says-europe-bought-320-billion-in-hydrocarbons-since-2022" /><summary type="html">Russia said on Monday that European Union countries had bought $320.7 billion worth of its energy resources since 2022, despite sanctions over the war in Ukraine. The figure fuelled tensions as European officials criticised a US deal to import Russian diesel, while Stockholm called for the bloc to use frozen Russian assets to boost support for Kyiv.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo diagnosed with lung cancer after doctors successfully remove nodule</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c42e19eb0ef8b76e69724141aab51d459427b0c2804c371ce459b5202e598646</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:53:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T22:20:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-what-we-know-about-pope-leo-xiv-planned-lung-operation-this-week--42462f7a7f54.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-what-we-know-about-pope-leo-xiv-planned-lung-operation-this-week" /><summary type="html">Pope ​Leo had a lower lobe ​of his right lung removed during surgery on Tuesday ​and ‌was diagnosed with lung ⁠adenocarcinoma, a common form of ‌lung cancer, the Vatican said in ⁠a medical bulletin. The surgery was successful and the pope is expected to spend a week in hospital recovering. The 71-year-old pontiff is due to travel to Uruguay, Argentina and Peru on November 6, though the Vatican has not confirmed the operation date.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'It's clear that Moscow is just playing with Washington,' analyst says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:20c9001ae0929e85d58a22e41c36ffee74d80b231a27bdda28530bdfc72442f5</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:53:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T21:02:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261012-it-s-clear-that-moscow-is-just-playing-with-washington-analyst-says--21ae94136adb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261012-it-s-clear-that-moscow-is-just-playing-with-washington-analyst-says" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump's envoys told ​Ukrainian officials on Friday that a deal to allow Russian diesel exports is part of a bid to draw Russia back to negotiations after the failure of previous efforts to launch sustained talks to end the war, three people familiar with the meeting told Reuters. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Grégoire Roos, director of the Europe and Russia and Eurasia Programmes at Chatham House. He says that "it's clear that Moscow is just playing with Washington because Vladimir Putin knows that Donald Trump lives on borrowed time".</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>'It's clear that Moscow is just playing with Washington,' analyst says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:730b57478246ec36bf78e4a3ddc9cd1f56e618fe20f40a46478cc27366ee0011</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:53:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T20:58:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/it-s-clear-that-moscow-is-just-playing-with-washington-analyst-says--518f477114b7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/it-s-clear-that-moscow-is-just-playing-with-washington-analyst-says" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump's envoys told ​Ukrainian officials on Friday that a deal to allow Russian diesel exports is part of a bid to draw Russia back to negotiations after the failure of previous efforts to launch sustained talks to end the war, three people familiar with the meeting told Reuters. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Grégoire Roos, director of the Europe and Russia and Eurasia Programmes at Chatham House. He says that "it's clear that Moscow is just playing with Washington because Vladimir Putin knows that Donald Trump lives on borrowed time".</summary></entry><entry><title>Tehran denies involvement in UK Fairford air base incident as Britain summons Iranian ambassador</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ce70e601ddc7662c79149afdde9904b8d9d1168993746293517781eec9f53e45</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:53:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T20:23:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-tehran-denies-involvement-in-uk-fairford-air-base-incident-as-britain-summons-iranian-ambas--9897b235b090.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-tehran-denies-involvement-in-uk-fairford-air-base-incident-as-britain-summons-iranian-ambassador" /><summary type="html">British Prime Minister Andy Burnham on Monday accused Iran's Revolutionary Guards of being responsible for a terror-related incident in September at England's Fairford air base, which is used by the United States military. Following Tehran's denial, the British Foreign Office summoned Iran's Ambassador for talks.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry></feed>
